parentage filter is the \verb{verify_parentage 3} default of preGSf90: a genotyped parent
and offspring with opposite homozygotes on more than \code{exclusion_threshold} of the
markers called in both cannot be parent and offspring, and the OFFSPRING's genotype is
dropped (preGSf90's \code{exclusion_threshold} is the same 1\%, over every SNP);
\code{\link[=parentage_check]{parentage_check()}} lists the pairs, for the alternative of setting the parent unknown
in the pedigree instead. Leave the sex-chromosome markers out of that test with
\verb{sex_markers =} (see \code{\link[=parentage_check]{parentage_check()}} for why).

